HST Office: the ribbon banner yields before a group collapses; a collapsed group shows its icon.

Owner report (13/11, HST Sheets at 1485 px): Styles and Cells showed as bare "Kiểu ▾" / "Ô ▾" text buttons
while the banner kept its 260 px slot.
- NotebookbarTabControl: besides the full width of every (non-contextual) tab page, the tab control keeps
  the width each page needs with its groups at their smallest state that is not the "Caption ▾" button
  (hst::ribbon::PageKeepWidth). When the widest of them does not fit beside the narrowest wide banner, the
  compact banner takes its place, and when it does not fit beside that either, the banner hides. So the
  order is: groups at full size, the wide banner narrows (360 -> 260 px), groups shrink by their ladders,
  the banner turns compact, then hides, and only then does a group collapse into its button.
- PriorityMergedHBox: a collapsed group's button shows the large icon of the group's first command
  (toolbox item or drop-down button; the caption's dialog launcher does not count) above "Caption ▾",
  as Office does, instead of bare text.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: build only (both files syntax-checked against the configured tree). Runtime: HST Sheets Home at 1366,
1440, 1485, 1536, 1600 and 1920 px shows no "Caption ▾" button while the banner is visible, and a collapsed
group shows an icon above its caption.
